From: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8750: set CPU interconnect paths as ACTIVE_ONLY

Port upstream commit 48c84d96dcd0 ("arm64: dts: qcom: sm8550: set CPU
interconnect paths as ACTIVE_ONLY") to SM8750. SM8550 and SM8650 already
tag every MASTER_APPSS_PROC path ACTIVE_ONLY; SM8750 still tags 42 of
them ALWAYS: the QUP config/I2C paths and the PCIe cpu-pcie path.

An ALWAYS tag copies the vote into the RPMh sleep set, so any of these
consumers left voting keeps the config NoC (CN0) and CX up after the CPU
subsystem collapses, even though the CPU cannot issue register accesses
while collapsed. ACTIVE_ONLY keeps the vote in the active and wake sets
only. The QUP and PCIe memory paths (to SLAVE_EBI1) keep their ALWAYS
tags, as on SM8550.
